From 2de5845da45b6b1aaced3794cc1aba12cebae4de Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Brent Kearney <1550934+brentkearney@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Thu, 17 Sep 2026 22:18:54 -0600
Subject: [PATCH 14/14] brcmfmac: gate the AWDL action-frame RX trace behind
 awdl_trace

The AWDL action-frame RX log line from the probe patches fires per frame.
A discoverable window sees PSFs and MIFs from every peer nearby, so a
release build would fill the kernel log with it.

The awdl_trace module parameter, off by default and writable at runtime
(0644), already exists upstream: it gates the tx-completion line in
msgbuf.c. Consult it here too, so one switch turns all the AWDL
per-frame tracing on and off:

  echo 1 > /sys/module/brcmfmac/parameters/awdl_trace

The rate limit stays; the parameter only decides whether it is consulted.

Signed-off-by: Brent Kearney <1550934+brentkearney@users.noreply.github.com>
---
 drivers/net/wireless/broadcom/brcm80211/brcmfmac/p2p.c | 2 +-
 1 file changed, 1 insertion(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/drivers/net/wireless/broadcom/brcm80211/brcmfmac/p2p.c b/drivers/net/wireless/broadcom/brcm80211/brcmfmac/p2p.c
index 05c1d90..0ffe241 100644
--- a/drivers/net/wireless/broadcom/brcm80211/brcmfmac/p2p.c
+++ b/drivers/net/wireless/broadcom/brcm80211/brcmfmac/p2p.c
@@ -1427,7 +1427,7 @@ int brcmf_p2p_notify_action_frame_rx(struct brcmf_if *ifp,
 		 * AWDL body by its signature and forward from there; dump the raw
 		 * head so the real header layout can be written down.
 		 */
-		if (__ratelimit(&awdl_af_rs))
+		if (brcmf_awdl_trace && __ratelimit(&awdl_af_rs))
 			pr_info("brcmfmac: awdl af rx from %pM datalen=%u reg=%04x head=%*phN\n",
 				e->addr, e->datalen,
 				ifp->vif ? ifp->vif->mgmt_rx_reg : 0,
